Thylacine: enable the built-in per-adjust cycle telemetry (cyclelog).

DOSBox-X's auto-cycle control loop (increaseticks() in src/dosbox.cpp) carries a
commented-out diagnostic that prints, once per ~250ms evaluation window, the
current CPU_CycleMax, the newly computed target, the control ratio, and the raw
ticksDone/ticksScheduled timing that drives the decision. Uncomment it.

It lives AFTER the `if (!CPU_CycleAutoAdjust) return;` guard, so it fires ONLY in
cycles=auto/max mode -- it is completely silent under a fixed cycles= setting (the
shipped Duke3D config). That makes it a zero-overhead opt-in instrument: run a game
with cycles=auto to observe the hunt, ship it with cycles=fixed to silence it.

Used to diagnose the Duke3D ~500ms turn-speed oscillation (the cycles=auto loop
hunting the emulated CPU speed) and to check whether Thylacine's host timer
resolution/jitter destabilises the loop more than a native host would.
--- a/src/dosbox.cpp	2026-09-04 14:35:55
+++ b/src/dosbox.cpp	2026-09-04 14:35:55
@@ -675,14 +675,12 @@
         if (new_cmax < CPU_CYCLES_LOWER_LIMIT)
             new_cmax = CPU_CYCLES_LOWER_LIMIT;
 
-        /*
            LOG_MSG("cyclelog: current %6d   cmax %6d   ratio  %5d  done %3d   sched %3d",
            CPU_CycleMax,
            new_cmax,
            ratio,
            ticksDone,
            ticksScheduled);
-           */
            /* ratios below 1% are considered to be dropouts due to
               temporary load imbalance, the cycles adjusting is skipped */
         if (ratio > 10) {
